 227: ## 5. Native macOS provisioning configuration
 228: 
 229: Extend `packaging/macos/guest/40-install-payload.sh`'s existing
 230: `install_canary_drop_in`; do not add a second drop-in. It should atomically
 231: write:
 232: 
 233: ```ini
 234: [Service]
 235: # Structural macOS/Lima gate ...
 236: Environment=IOLBOX_DISABLE_I386=1
 237: ExecStartPre=/opt/iolbox-provision/30-canary.sh --quiet
 238: ```
 239: 
 240: One file is preferable because both lines express the same qualified Mac
 241: runtime invariant, are installed before the payload's first start, share the
 242: existing attestation/verification path, and cannot drift independently by
 243: drop-in ordering. Do not replace or repeat the base `ExecStart`.
 244: 
 245: Enhance `verify_gated_unit` to inspect both human-readable `systemctl cat` and
 246: effective `systemctl show -p Environment -p ExecStartPre -p ExecStart`. Extend
 247: `50-verify.sh` with a correlated hello read (do not assume the first NDJSON
 248: frame is the reply) and require: `i386` absent and
 249: `iolArchitectures:["x86_64"]` present. Add the effective capability signal to
 250: the fact block/evidence.
 251: 
 252: An in-place upgrade proceeds as M1 proved: the provisioner stops any ungated
 253: service, runs the canary, atomically rewrites the same drop-in including the
 254: environment line, daemon-reloads, then runs the native installer. The
 255: installer may overwrite the base unit; it does not overwrite the drop-in.
 256: After the gated restart, effective-unit and hello verification must pass before
 257: the structural attestation is mirrored host-side. Images, labs, iourc, and
 258: cache are untouched.
