 260: ## 6. Launcher diagnostics: measured values only
 261: 
 262: Remove the hardcoded lines at `macos_cli.go:276`. Refactor status and diagnose
 263: to share a small diagnostic snapshot helper, with unit-testable parsing and
 264: formatting. Both commands print these exact keys, one per line:
 265: 
 266: ```text
 267: guest_arch=<value>
 268: execution=<value>
 269: guest_kernel=<value>
 270: structural_canary=<value>
 271: ```
 272: 
 273: Measurement sources:
 274: 
 275: - `guest_arch`: live `limactl shell <machine> uname -m`.
 276: - `guest_kernel`: live `uname -r`.
 277: - `structural_canary`: the latest guest
 278:   `/var/lib/iolbox/macos-canary.json` verdict/timestamp, cross-checked with the
 279:   configured `ExecStartPre`; when the guest cannot be queried, clearly label
 280:   the host-mirrored `<machine>-structural-gate.json` value as the **last
 281:   attested** result rather than current state.
 282: - `execution`: report `rosetta-amd64` only when all measured facts agree:
 283:   guest arch is `aarch64`; the live binfmt entry is enabled and names
 284:   `/mnt/lima-rosetta/rosetta`; the canary record is PASS for amd64 loader
 285:   execution; and the supervisor service/hello is reachable. Otherwise print
 286:   `unknown (<specific failed predicate>)`. A configured
 287:   `IOLBOX_DISABLE_I386=1` is never an input to this value.
 288: 
 289: `diagnose` retains its raw binfmt, effective drop-in, service, HTTP, hello, and
 290: live-canary detail after the four summary keys. Its live canary line remains
 291: `live_canary=PASS` or `live_canary=FAIL (<error>)`; it must not promote a
 292: failed live canary to `execution=rosetta-amd64`. It also prints
 293: `capability_policy=PASS` only when the effective environment and hello agree,
 294: otherwise `capability_policy=FAIL (<reason>)`.
 295: 
 296: Unavailable-state contract:
 297: 
 298: | Situation | `guest_arch` / `guest_kernel` | `execution` | `structural_canary` |
 299: |---|---|---|---|
 300: | Machine not created or stopped | `unavailable (machine is not running)` | same | `PASS (last attested <timestamp>)` if a valid host mirror exists, otherwise `unknown (never recorded)` |
 301: | Lima says running but guest shell is unreachable | `unavailable (guest unreachable: <error>)` | `unknown (guest unreachable)` | last host-attested value, explicitly labelled, or `unknown (never recorded)` |
 302: | Canary has never run | live arch/kernel still print if reachable | `unknown (no passing Rosetta canary record)` | `unknown (never recorded)` |
 303: | Live facts disagree or canary failed | measured arch/kernel print | `unknown (<mismatch/failure>)` | the actual non-PASS verdict and timestamp |
 304: 
 305: Do not print the profile's expected arch/kernel as if measured. Existing
 306: `kernel pin:` and profile facts may remain, but must stay separately labelled
 307: as expectations.
 308: 
 309: ## 7. Blast-radius matrix
 310: 
 311: No runtime packer, rootfs, Dockerfile, Docker entrypoint, or non-Mac systemd
 312: unit changes for M5. Every target receives the updated supervisor binary/GUI
 313: when rebuilt, but only the Mac drop-in supplies the switch.
 314: 
 315: | Target sharing the supervisor | Signal present? | Hello/features | Image execution and GUI |
 316: |---|---|---|---|
 317: | Apple Silicon Lima/VZ + Rosetta | Yes, from macOS guest provisioning | omits `i386`; adds `iolArchitectures:["x86_64"]`; existing runtime `arch` stays `x86_64` | i386 shown unsupported and server-rejected; x86_64 unchanged |
 318: | WSL2 rootfs | No | default hello remains legacy-shaped and includes `i386` | unchanged |
 319: | VMware vmdk/vmx appliance | No | includes `i386` | unchanged |
 320: | OVA imported into VMware/ESXi/VirtualBox | No | includes `i386` | unchanged; it is the same appliance rootfs in another package |
 321: | Proxmox LXC template | No | includes `i386` | unchanged |
 322: | Native systemd x86-64 Linux: bare metal, cloud VM, on-prem guest | No; `/etc/iolbox/bind.env` is not changed | includes `i386` | unchanged |
 323: | QEMU qcow2 used by the Windows launcher/qemu-compat provider | No | includes `i386` | unchanged |
 324: | Docker build-from-source target | No; it execs the supervisor directly and has no systemd drop-in | includes `i386` | unchanged |
 325: 
 326: Concrete non-Mac checks:
 327: 
 328: 1. On the Windows dev host, run the cross-platform server tests, especially
 329:    `TestHelloDefaultAdvertisesI386`; this pins the no-signal default without
 330:    requiring Linux data-plane privileges.
 331: 2. On an actual amd64 Linux deployment, install/start the M5 payload **without**
 332:    setting `IOLBOX_DISABLE_I386`, then send a correlated hello to
 333:    `127.0.0.1:4000` and save the reply. Require `features` to contain `i386`,
 334:    require `iolArchitectures` to be absent, and start one i386 image if a legal
 335:    test image is available.
 336: 
 337: No usable non-Mac deployment is currently known from this planning session:
 338: Docker is unavailable and WSL enumeration returns
 339: `Wsl/EnumerateDistros/Service/E_ACCESSDENIED`. The owner must either provide an
 340: amd64 Linux target or approve an ephemeral CI/native-Linux smoke. This is a
 341: real-hardware acceptance blocker for the non-Mac criterion, not something a
 342: Mac SSH run can prove.
