tools/iolab-launcher/README.md:40: 
tools/iolab-launcher/README.md:41: - **`images\`** â€” drop `.bin`/`.iol` IOL image files here. Each launch, every
tools/iolab-launcher/README.md:42:   image in this folder is uploaded to the guest and registered into the image
tools/iolab-launcher/README.md:43:   registry, so it shows up in the GUI's image picker. Images are re-synced
tools/iolab-launcher/README.md:44:   (re-uploaded + re-registered) on **every** launch, since the guest's
tools/iolab-launcher/README.md:45:   registry doesn't persist either.
tools/iolab-launcher/README.md:46: - **`labs\`** â€” saved labs persist here as `<labId>.json`. On launch, every
tools/iolab-launcher/README.md:47:   `.json` file here is pushed into the guest. While iolbox is running, any lab
tools/iolab-launcher/README.md:48:   you create or edit in the GUI is written back to this folder automatically
tools/iolab-launcher/README.md:49:   (every 30 seconds, and once more on shutdown) â€” so your work is never lost
tools/iolab-launcher/README.md:50:   when the guest disk resets.
tools/iolab-launcher/README.md:51: 
tools/iolab-launcher/README.md:52: Both folders are created automatically on first launch if missing; their
tools/iolab-launcher/README.md:53: absolute paths are logged at startup.
tools/iolab-launcher/README.md:54: 
tools/iolab-launcher/README.md:55: The guest ships with its own built-in starter labs, re-seeded every boot.
tools/iolab-launcher/README.md:56: These are never written into `labs\` and are never overwritten by a
tools/iolab-launcher/README.md:57: same-named file you place there.
tools/iolab-launcher/README.md:58: 
